  "accounting": "Scratch 224 MiB plus shm 32 MiB are user-mounted regular storage limits. Runtime-managed /dev must be a separate 64 MiB tmpfs, root-owned mode 0755, with usable /dev/null; no custom /dev mount or invented inode cap. Its observed inode count must be positive and is recorded only in failure/success inspection, not claimed configured. Nonroot cannot create regular files in /dev itself. devpts/PTY and device operations are not regular-file capacity; IPC creation syscalls remain denied. Anonymous and kernel memory accounting depends on verified 4 GiB cgroup memory/no-swap and actual platform support; this narrow synthetic pilot is not blanket containment proof. No cumulative-write or universal 256 MiB claim."
